I read the delivery in the checkout (`opencode.json`, both phase documents, all three test files) and the checkout's own git metadata.

FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] phases/phase-084/REPORT.md:39 — The round-7 account of the change set omits a file the delivery carries, and the inherited-state sentence above the round-7 table is false. REPORT.md:39 says "This run inherited round 6's delivery **committed** (`HEAD` is `1b58178`) and the two delivery documents uncommitted", but the checkout's own reflog shows exactly one commit since the clone: `.git/logs/HEAD:2` is `b21821d → 1b58178  commit: resume phase-084: adopt preserved work`, and `.git/logs/HEAD:3-15` are thirteen `reset: moving to HEAD` entries with old==new — no commit was ever made after `1b58178`. By the report's own account (REPORT.md:650) `1b58178` is "the commit that adopted rounds 4 and 5's work", so round 6's delivery is **not** in HEAD; it is still sitting uncommitted in the working tree. That is visible in the diff handed to this review: `tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs` is modified (+11/−3) in the uncommitted delta, and that is exactly the acknowledgement repoint the round-6 table describes at REPORT.md:744 ("repointed from `d23068b` … to `1b58178`"). REPORT.md:755-765 accordingly describes round 7's diff as "**one rule and two tests** in the phase's own config suite, plus the two documents" and lists three files, while the delivery's diff carries four. Why it matters: "What changed" is the phase's own account of what it ships; it hides that a fourth file moves, and it states the inherited state as committed when it is not, so the acknowledgement treadmill's next payment is attributed to the wrong round — the report's "the tenth payment falls due to the next run" (REPORT.md:131) reads as though this delivery carried no acknowledgement edit, when it is this delivery's own uncommitted `+11/−3` that keeps the gate green today. Fix: correct REPORT.md:39 to say round 6's delivery was inherited *uncommitted* (HEAD = `1b58178` carries rounds 4–5 only), add a `tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs` row to the round-7 table marked inherited-uncommitted (the shape round 4's table uses at REPORT.md:697), and restate the diff sentence to name four files. VERIFIED: read `.git/logs/HEAD` (lines 1–15) and the change set's committed/uncommitted numstat in the review request; cross-read REPORT.md:39, :650, :744, :755-765 and `tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs:118-131` (the entry naming `1b58178` and saying it "replaces the `d23068b` entry").
2. [MINOR] phases/phase-084/REPORT.md:368 — The documents still claim the document-suite guard "reads `HEAD`'s committed report and fails against it" (REPORT.md:368; FINDINGS.md:1379-1381), but `tests/report_markdown_test.rs:85-88` reads the **working tree** copy (`fs::read_to_string` of `<repo>/phases/phase-084/<name>`), so the guard can never fail because of HEAD's copy — it fails when the working-tree document is broken, and a committed report that is broken while the working-tree copy is fixed stays green. This is the third statement of the same claim: round 5's review raised it ("neither reads the report") and the fix renamed the tests but kept the wording. Fix: say the test reads the working-tree copy; if HEAD's copy is what must be guarded, assert against `git show HEAD:phases/phase-084/REPORT.md` instead.
3. [MINOR] phases/phase-084/REPORT.md:847 — Round 7's pipeline half is asserted but unverifiable from this checkout: commit `52bdf9e` (`rbops/dispatch.sh` +19/−4, `rbops/smoke.sh` +11) and the "232 checks, green" figure live in the pipeline repo, one directory up, outside the checkout, and this reviewer's own permissions deny `external_directory`, so **I could not check it**. Nothing in this delivery fails if that commit does not exist: no project test reads the pipeline repo, and the report's own Known gaps (REPORT.md:1704-1715) says the same of the pipeline's `opencode.json`. This phase has twice reported pipeline work that was not there — round 3's fix died in the pipeline's working tree, and round 4's report claimed it had been done, which the next review called a BLOCKER. What would settle it: `git -C ../rbops show 52bdf9e` and `bash ../rbops/smoke.sh` pasted into the report, or an explicit note that the figure is a measurement from outside the checkout that this repository cannot gate.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 3
